Z||000005||Tigger||08-22-2001||01:09 PM||||Replacing the line isn't a tough job and it would save you the $ for a tow.  If you replace the line yourself, you will need to punch in the center and drill out the big momma rivit that holds the line to the upper control arm.  I'd recommend replacing this with another rivit.  You can get the car to a shop using a medium/heavy electrical tie and have them replace the rivit for a few bucks.||||reg||1
